{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1142844-building-a-new-chronicle-advice-requested","id":1142844,"title":"Building a new chronicle [advice requested]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-22T02:27:16-07:00","id":1142844,"title":"Building a new chronicle [advice requested]","content":"Seeing as how Changeling: the Lost 2nd Edition will (fingers crossed) be available sometime next year I'm starting to build a chronicle. The deadline is for September 2018.<br /> <br /> Here is the inspirational start to my very first war-story using the Storyteller system. I'll be taking a closer look at WoD: Dogs of War and CofD: Hurt Locker for ideas, but this is a story about the Lost.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fall of a Gossamer Kingdom</span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dead kingdom falls</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These are the final nights of its decline</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the way we fight back</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the cold iron with which we strike</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All through the sleepless nights</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warmed with hope and steadied by conviction</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruled by its passions the True Fae falls</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Desire is the way to unite us against the master</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wrath is the way to bring ruin upon the master\u2019s works</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fear is the way to break the master\u2019s servants</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorrow is the way to mourn the fallen soldiers after victory</span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> The main question on my mind is: one or more Keepers? The whole idea behind the chronicle is that a Keeper has come to dominate a portion of London (1862) and has created its personal kingdom there. Now the local Freehold, and others besides, want to kick that Keeper out. Bring down the Gossamer Kingdom. Originally I was thinking that there would only be the one Keeper. Of course there would be multiple Keepers in the background of the story, but those would serve only as minor subplots at best. This would provide a clear and easily recognizable target to war against. A black and white case of striking down the Keeper. The moral conundrums would revolve around other things besides the Keeper, who is obviously Evil.<br /> <br /> From a storytelling perspective a strong, easily identifiable and memorable villain is desirable. However, I find the idea of a single Keeper to be a little one-note. You can't really reason with the thing can you? At best you can make a deal that delays the inevitable. Sooner or later the Keeper no longer finds you useful and off to Arcadia you go unless you manage to escape. The story of every Loyalist and Privateer. The question is: what would a second or a third Keeper bring to the story?<br /> <br /> I have been playing around with the idea of highlighting the tragedy of war through extremes. The Mad, Militia, Bridge-Burners, Loyalists and Privateers. I can get some really tragic stories out of those basic concepts.This brings me back to the same question: what would I get out of adding a second or third Keeper? A single Keeper will keep focus on it. A steady build up of conflict towards the inevitable final showdown that no one can ignore. All or nothing: either the Keeper is driven out or the Lost will be crushed.<br /> <br /> It's a simple story, which allows a lot of maneuverability while marching towards the unavoidable conclusion. Or, is it unavoidable? Maybe there's an alternative way to defeat the Evil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","user":"TelperionST","date":". 09-22-2017, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T07:14:28-07:00","id":1142889,"title":"","content":"Well, you could always have one Keeper <i>known</i>, and one or more come along or discovered later. The Gentry Feud among themselves. Maybe the war is emphasized by another &quot;foreign&quot; Other waging war upon the main one. Or the primary Keeper imprisoned their predecessor, and could be freed to turn against their former captor. Or an interloper seeks to enlist the Freehold to help steal a Title from the main Keeper.<br /> <br /> Always the question - is the new Gentry any real Improvement over the old one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T09:47:28-07:00","id":1142940,"title":"","content":"you know, you can have the best of both worlds. True Fae are less people and more a collection of narratives wrapped around a beating cyst of the Wyrd guided by an overarching mythology. remember, the majority of changelings aren't aware of the true nature of their Keepers. Two changelings could be kept by a singular Faery, yet interact with different manifestations of its panoply of Titles and believe that they were enslaved by two disparate entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T13:15:47-07:00","id":1143302,"title":"","content":"If you want to add some complexity to your narrative without deviating too far from the central theme of reclaiming this piece of London from the Fae you could have a second Keeper attempting to steal the kingdom when the Changelings topple the first one but before they can recover from that ordeal enough to fend off a coup. How do you avoid being pawns of a greater actor? How do you ensure all your hard work has its desired end and doesn't just pave the way for a worse enemy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T23:00:08-07:00","id":1143681,"title":"","content":"The question of having a conflict amongst the Gentry is a given, but what does it really bring to the story? A new layer of complexity in an otherwise already complex storyline. I would also rather not bring in a second boss, a stronger one at that, into the game towards the game. I want to give the players a sense of conclusion that's at least partially satisfying. Including a second, bigger, Keeper would also mean that they come with a lot more resources at a time when the players are going to be burning through a lot of their own resources. I really don't like leaving things at a cliffhanger, which is why I would rather not do that.<br /> <br /> The different aspects idea is a good one, though. I can make the players believe that there are two Keepers, when in reality there's only one. Make it part of the story from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T03:20:12-07:00","id":1143716,"title":"","content":"Here's what I wrote above written in a different way.<br /> <br /> I want to make a promise to every player who participates in the chronicle that they are going to experience (through their character) struggle, danger, action and difficult choices. At the end of that journey they are going to get a fair chance at winning. They can't expect with 100% certainty that they are going to win, but they can at least expect to have better than even odds of winning. They are most likely going to win. So, there's a payoff to joining, because of the expected ending. The players don't know how this is going to come about, they can look forward to a satisfying ending.<br /> <br /> Except, and here's the important part, they might lose. Now, adding in a second Keeper, late in the game, just to ramp up the difficulty is going to feel like cheating. After all that hard work the players are going to have to deal with another threat that they probably don't have the necessary resources to deal with. Or, they will be stretched out to the maximum. While this can create great tension, I'm going to err on the side of caution and assume it's just going to be frustrating to most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T03:43:55-07:00","id":1143720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1142844-building-a-new-chronicle-advice-requested?p=1143716#post1143716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's what I wrote above written in a different way.<br /> <br /> I want to make a promise to every player who participates in the chronicle that they are going to experience (through their character) struggle, danger, action and difficult choices. At the end of that journey they are going to get a fair chance at winning. They can't expect with 100% certainty that they are going to win, but they can at least expect to have better than even odds of winning. They are most likely going to win. So, there's a payoff to joining, because of the expected ending. The players don't know how this is going to come about, they can look forward to a satisfying ending.<br /> <br /> Except, and here's the important part, they might lose. Now, adding in a second Keeper, late in the game, just to ramp up the difficulty is going to feel like cheating. After all that hard work the players are going to have to deal with another threat that they probably don't have the necessary resources to deal with. Or, they will be stretched out to the maximum. While this can create great tension, I'm going to err on the side of caution and assume it's just going to be frustrating to most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well depending on where and when you introduce a second Gentry, it might make their immediate goals <i>easier</i>. After all, when their main target is now diverting resources to fight another Keeper, the Changeling PCs have to face less resistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T04:37:56-07:00","id":1143731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1142844-building-a-new-chronicle-advice-requested?p=1143720#post1143720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well depending on where and when you introduce a second Gentry, it might make their immediate goals <i>easier</i>. After all, when their main target is now diverting resources to fight another Keeper, the Changeling PCs have to face less resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, essentially, the players get to choose which Keeper they would rather have as their final boss? They see these two powerful beings going at it, they may get an opportunity to learn more details about one or the other as the story goes along and then finally they run into a point of no return. One of those Keepers is going to win and whoever is left standing is going to keep doing evil, unacceptable things.<br /> <br /> This is an idea that I could work with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Tallenna</span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T04:45:02-07:00","id":1143736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1142844-building-a-new-chronicle-advice-requested?p=1143731#post1143731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, essentially, the players get to choose which Keeper they would rather have as their final boss? They see these two powerful beings going at it, they may get an opportunity to learn more details about one or the other as the story goes along and then finally they run into a point of no return. One of those Keepers is going to win and whoever is left standing is going to keep doing evil, unacceptable things.<br /> <br /> This is an idea that I could work with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Tallenna</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The other Keeper might even be amenable to deals, making them a &quot;barely tolerable evil&quot;, should the Players want to got that route. Or, if they are truly ambitious, let both sides weaken the other and try to take out the victor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T06:04:20-07:00","id":1143749,"title":"","content":"Of course, that means both sides are kidnapping and buying more human cannon fodder from the Goblin Market to participate in their war. So letting the war go on puts that on your conscience. Fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T07:57:25-07:00","id":1143785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1142844-building-a-new-chronicle-advice-requested?p=1143749#post1143749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that means both sides are kidnapping and buying more human cannon fodder from the Goblin Market to participate in their war. So letting the war go on puts that on your conscience. Fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are also Thralls for sale from some rather shady nomadic Goblin Merchants, who are attracted to such events for profit and finding new customers of opportunity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T10:09:39-07:00","id":1143831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1142844-building-a-new-chronicle-advice-requested?p=1143785#post1143785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are also Thralls for sale from some rather shady nomadic Goblin Merchants, who are attracted to such events for profit and finding new customers of opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shady would imply that slavery wasn't a respected business opportunity at the Goblin Market","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}